// 1. PROFILE: async-profiler (CPU + alloc), or JFR.

// 3. ONE CHANGE at the measured hotspot. The Kotlin-specific wins:

//    a. avoid a per-call lambda allocation in a hot loop (use `inline`):
inline fun <T> List<T>.sumFast(): Long { var s = 0L; for (x in this) s += x; return s }
//       `forEach { }` on a non-inline receiver allocates a Function per call;
//       the stdlib marks withLock/let/run/apply `inline` for exactly this.

//    b. avoid boxing: List<Int> boxes each element, IntArray does not.
val arr = IntArray(n); var s = 0; for (x in arr) s += x     // no boxing, contiguous

//    c. avoid a Sequence in a hot loop: it allocates an iterator per stage.
//       for (x in list) { ... } is cheaper than list.asSequence().map{}.filter{}

